{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And you shall command</b> — Moses is not mentioned in this sidra, unlike the entire Torah, where from the time Moses was born there is no sidra in which he is not mentioned (aside from Deuteronomy). The reason: because he said, \"blot me out, I pray, from Your book which You have written,\" and the curse of a sage, even on a condition, comes and is fulfilled here. And he wrote צוואה (command/testament) regarding the Menorah and likewise regarding the daily offering, \"Command the children of Israel,\" because both are practiced every day and involve expenditure of money, therefore they require urging, therefore the language of צוואה is used for them. תצוה in gematria = נשים צוה — a hint that lighting the lamp for women is an obligation on Shabbat." "<b>And they shall take to you</b> — but I do not need its light." "<b>Beaten</b> — a hint: ת\"י ת\"כ — two; the kindling of the Menorah shall be practiced." "<b>A perpetual lamp</b> — in gematria: בשבת."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:33.231975001Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}